usage: slopmop <folder> [section ...] [--intelfile <file>]

reads a folder and everything below it, runs nothing, and prints the whole analysis

sections (name any to print only those; none = all):
  summary      the counts
  timeline     each file in order, with what it shows
  findings     each activity, indicator and tactic, most severe first
  files        the files that hold a finding of high severity
  impact       what the findings mean
  remediation  what to do about them, most urgent first
  mitigation   what MITRE ATT&CK and ATLAS say prevents the techniques found

params (double dash, take a value):
  --intelfile  <file>

one view as a table or as JSON: slopmop NOUN VERB [selectors] [--params] [output flags] [positional]

nouns:
  file, files          files in the input directory
  trace, traces        script trace of the input directory
  finding, findings    detections aggregated from the trace
  report, reports      report on an analysis of the input directory
  campaign, campaigns  campaigns named in a threat intelligence watchlist

more help: slopmop NOUN -h, slopmop NOUN VERB -h
